<title>GERMANY: Victoria expects higher 1997 earnings.</title>
<headline>Victoria expects higher 1997 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>German insurance group Victoria said on Wednesday that it expected earnings to improve in full-year 1997, despite a difficult market situation.</p>
<p>In the first five months of 1997, consolidated premium income was, as expected, slightly below that of the same time last year. This was in particular due to intense competition for motor insurance in the German market, the group said.</p>
<p>Victoria reported a group net profit of 116 million marks.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
